<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stolac</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stolac is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>, in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and Herzegovina, on the Bregava river. Its surroundings are rich in archaeological remains, including the Illyrian hillfort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daorson">Daorson</a> and the medieval necropolis of Radimlja, whose decorated tombstones (stećci) are part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> World Heritage listing. The town's Ottoman mosques and bridges were badly damaged in the war of the 1990s and have since been restored.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stolac.jpg" alt="Stolac" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Golden Bosnian Lily · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stolac_(collage).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
